From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: GPU DVFS at stock's points, PLL_GPU pinned at 600 MHz

0024e gave the GPU operating points of 288, 432, 600 and 696 MHz, the
points PLL_GPU makes with M = 1. With PLL_GPU's output divider unmodelled
(the preceding clk patch, 0268), every one of them ran at half its name:
Panfrost's cycle counters measured 144, 216, 300 and 348 MHz at those four
points (HY310, 12.10.2026, mean over 10 s windows, Mali counters and CCU
registers agree).

PLL_GPU is now pinned at 600 MHz by assigned-clock-rates. The table is
600 MHz divided by the GPU clock's M divider (150/200/300/600), so a DVFS
step never relocks the PLL; see 0268. Stock holds PLL_GPU at exactly
600 MHz in every capture and lists these four points for this die. Every
point is 960 mV, the fixed vdd_sys, which is the voltage stock gives every
GPU point.

This raises the GPU's real ceiling from 348 MHz (696 MHz as claimed) to
600 MHz.

The original patch also gave gpu-thermal a passive trip at 85 C, a
critical trip at 105 C and a cooling map onto the GPU's devfreq cooling
device. 0024e already carries all three with the same temperatures, so
that part is not repeated.

Adapted for this series from the original: its message is kept and
shortened where 0024e already did the work; the OPP table replaces
0024e's instead of being added beside it (the original does not apply on
top of 0024e: it declares gpu_opp_table a second time); the
assigned-clocks hunk is rewritten against this tree.

Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/kernel/0153-arm64-dts-h713-gpu-dvfs-and-thermal-throttling.patch (0153-arm64-dts-h713-gpu-dvfs-and-thermal-throttling.patch, adapted)
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -360,34 +360,37 @@
 
 	/* Thermal zones for CPU thermal management */
 	/*
-	 * GPU operating points. The stock DTB's gpu-opp-table tops out at
-	 * 700 MHz; without a table of our own Panfrost ran the core at the
-	 * PLL's boot rate of 864 MHz, fixed - panfrost_devfreq_init returns
-	 * early with -ENODEV, so there was no devfreq and no cooling device.
-	 * These four points are what PLL-GPU makes with M = 1 (24 MHz x N):
-	 * 288, 432, 600, 696 MHz. The rail is the fixed 0.96 V vdd_sys, so
-	 * every point names that voltage and the regulator call is a no-op.
-	 * The exact stock points (150 .. 348, 600, 700 MHz) would need the
-	 * gpu clock's M divider modelled in the CCU - later, if the
-	 * measurements ask for it.
+	 * GPU DVFS, frequency only. vdd_sys is fixed at 960 mV, the voltage
+	 * stock gives every GPU point. PLL_GPU is held at 600 MHz -- what the
+	 * vendor stack programs (0xb8001800 in every CCU capture) -- and the
+	 * points are 600 MHz / M, the GPU clock's own 2-bit divider, so DVFS
+	 * never relocks the PLL. They are the stock table's points for this
+	 * die; stock runs the top one with DVFS off.
+	 *
+	 * Before 0268 the GPU ran at half of what clk_summary claimed: PLL_GPU's
+	 * output divider was not modelled, so the 288..696 MHz points of 0024e
+	 * were really 144..348 MHz (measured, HY310, 12.10.2026).
 	 */
 	gpu_opp_table: opp-table-gpu {
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
-		opp-288000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <288000000>;
+		opp-150000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <150000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
 		};
-		opp-432000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <432000000>;
+
+		opp-200000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <200000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
 		};
-		opp-600000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+
+		opp-300000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <300000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
 		};
-		opp-696000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <696000000>;
+
+		opp-600000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <960000>;
 		};
 	};
@@ -1467,6 +1470,8 @@
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_GPU>, <&ccu CLK_BUS_GPU>;
 			clock-names = "core", "bus";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GPU>;
+			assigned-clocks = <&ccu CLK_PLL_GPU>;
+			assigned-clock-rates = <600000000>;
 			operating-points-v2 = <&gpu_opp_table>;
 			mali-supply = <&reg_vdd_sys>;
 			/*
